==English==
{{wikipedia|go (verb)|go}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰeh₁-|*wendʰ-}}
From {{inh-lite|en|enm|gon}}, {{m-lite|enm|goon}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gān|t=to go}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gān}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gāną|t=to go}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰeh₁-|t=to leave}}.

The inherited past tense form {{m-lite|en|yode}} (compare {{cog|ang|ēode}}) was replaced through [[suppletion]] in the 15th century by {{m-lite|en|went}}, from {{cog-lite|ang|wendan||to go, depart, wend}}.

{{rel-top|cognates and related terms}}
Cognate with {{cog-lite|sco|gae||to go}}, {{cog-lite|fy|gean||to go}}, {{cog-lite|nl|gaan||to go}}, {{cog-lite|nds|gahn||to go}}, {{cog-lite|de|gehen||to go}}, {{cog-lite|sv|-}} and {{cog|da|gå|t=to go}}, {{cog|no|gå|t=to walk}}. Compare also {{cog-lite|sq|ngah||to run, drive, go}}, {{cog|grc|κιχάνω|t=to meet with, arrive at}}, {{cog|ae|𐬰𐬀𐬰𐬁𐬨𐬌}}, {{cog|sa|जहाति|tr=jáhāti}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

