# {{i|used as an auxiliary time verb for perfect (tense) sentences; placed after verb {{l-lite|gsw|sii||being}} and causing an omission of participle {{l-lite|gsw|gange||went}}}}

===Etymology 2===
{{root|gsw|ine-pro|*ǵʰeh₁-|*ǵʰengʰ-}}
Cognate to (verb) {{cog-lite|gsw|gon||go}}, {{m-lite|gsw|ga}}, {{m-lite|gsw|gan}}, etc. From {{inh|gsw|gmh|gān}} ({{m|gmh|gēn}}), from {{inh|gsw|goh|gān}}, ({{m|goh|gēn}}), from {{inh|gsw|gmw-pro|*gān}}, from {{inh|gsw|gem-pro|*gāną}}, from {{inh|gsw|ine-pro|*ǵʰeh₁-||to leave}}. Cognate with {{cog-lite|de|gehen}}, {{cog-lite|nds|gan}}, {{m-lite|nds|gahn}}, {{cog-lite|nl|gaan}}, {{cog-lite|en|go}}, Danish and {{cog|sv|gå}}.

Not to be confused with the particle/preposition {{l-lite|gsw|go||to, towards}} ({{l-lite|gsw|ga}}, {{l-lite|gsw|ge}}, etc.).

