From {{inh-lite|ga|sga|co}}, from {{inh|ga|ine-pro|*ḱóm||next to, at, with, along}}. Cognate with {{cog-lite|de|ge-||with}} (collective prefix) and {{m-lite|de|gegen||toward, against}}, {{cog-lite|en|gain-}}, {{cog-lite|es|con||with}}, {{cog|ru|ко||to}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA-lite|ga|/ɡɔ/|/ɡə/}}<ref>{{R:ga:SjPh|88}}</ref>

===Conjunction===
{{head-lite|ga|conjunctions}} {{q-lite|triggers {{ga-mut-link|e}}, takes dependent form of irregular verbs}}

# [[that]] {{q-lite|used to introduce a [[subordinate clause]]}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Deir sé '''go''' bhfuil [[deifir]] air.|He says that he is in a hurry.}}
# {{n-g-lite|used to introduce a subjunctive hortative}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|'''Go''' [[cuidigh|gcuidí]] [[Dia]] leo.|May God help them.}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|'''Go''' maire tú é!|May you live to enjoy it!}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|'''Go''' raibh maith agat.|Thank you.|lit=May you have good.}}
# [[until]], [[till]]
#: {{syn-lite|ga|go dtí go}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Fan '''go''' dtiocfaidh sé.|Wait until he comes.}}

====Related terms====
* {{sense-lite|introducing subordinate clause; until}}
** {{l-lite|ga|gur}} {{q-lite|for past tenses}}
** {{l-lite|ga|nach}} {{q-lite|for negated clauses}}
** {{l|ga|nár}} {{q-lite|for past tenses in negated clauses}}
* {{sense-lite|introducing subjunctive hortative}} {{l|ga|nár}} {{q-lite|for a negative wish}}

===Preposition===
{{ga-prep|d|h}}

# [[to]] (with places), [[till]], [[until]]
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|dul '''go''' Meiriceá|to go to America}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Fáilte '''go''' hÉirinn|Welcome to Ireland}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|'''go''' leor|enough, plenty, galore|lit=until plenty}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|'''go''' fóill|still, yet, till later, in a while, later on}}

====Usage notes====
* In the meaning "to", used with place names that do not start with the definite article. Place names that do start with the definite article use {{m|ga|go dtí}} instead. In a few fixed phrases, the archaic form {{m-lite|ga|gos}} is used.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ga|go dtí}}

===Particle===
{{head-lite|ga|particles}} {{q-lite|triggers {{ga-mut-link|h}}}}

# {{n-g-lite|used to make temporary state [[adverb]]s}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|D’ith sé '''go''' maith.|He ate well.}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Shiúlaíodar '''go''' mall.|They walked slowly.}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|'''go''' feargach|angrily}}
# {{n-g-lite|used to make [[predicative]] [[adjective]]s expressing an [[opinion]] or [[value judgment]]}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Tá an t-anraith seo '''go''' maith.|This soup is good.}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Bhí a mac '''go''' hálainn.|Her son was beautiful.}}
#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Ní raibh an film '''go''' huafásach.|The film wasn't awful.}}

====Usage notes====
Only used with predicate adjectives expressing a value judgment like "good/bad", "beautiful/ugly" etc. Other predicate adjectives do not take a particle:
: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Tá an t-anraith seo te.|This soup is hot.}}
: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Bhí a mac ard.|Her son was tall.}}
: {{ux-lite|inline=1|ga|Ní raibh an film fada.|The film wasn't long.}}

